<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dezful</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dezful is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> province, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, on the Dez river at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains. It grew around an ancient bridge across the river, built in the Sasanian period, from which it takes its name. Nearby lie the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chogha-zanbil">Chogha Zanbil</a>, and the surrounding region was part of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dezful.jpg" alt="Dezful" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mansor110 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A2%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%85%DA%AF%D8%A7%D9%87_%DB%8C%D8%B9%D9%82%D9%88%D8%A8_%D9%84%DB%8C%D8%AB_%D8%B5%D9%81%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%8C%D8%A7%D9%88%D9%84%DB%8C%D9%86_%D8%B4%D9%87%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%B1_%D8%A7%DB%8C%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%86%DB%8C_%D8%A8%D8%B9%D8%AF_%D8%A7%D8%B2_%D8%A7%D8%B3%D9%84%D8%A7%D9%857.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
